      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-4">RackNerd Fall Giveaway 2026: Free VPS + Meta Quest 3</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-400 text-lg mb-6">RackNerd's Fall 2026 giveaway includes a Meta Quest 3, Synology NAS, and 5 free VPS. We checked the real cost of their $21.99/yr deals vs Hostinger BF.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <span class="text-xs text-gray-400 bg-white/5 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-white/10">RackNerd</span>
        <span class="text-xs text-gray-400 bg-white/5 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-white/10">Giveaway</span>
        <span class="text-xs text-gray-400 bg-white/5 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-white/10">Black Friday</span>
        <span class="text-xs text-gray-400 bg-white/5 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-white/10">VPS Deals</span>
        <span class="text-xs text-gray-400 bg-white/5 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-white/10">Hostinger</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
    <article class="prose prose-invert max-w-none">

      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-6">Last verified: November 9, 2026. We fetched the LowEndBox article published November 8, pinged racknerd.com (7.8ms avg, 0% loss), and pulled Hostinger's live pricing page to cross-check the TechRadar BF claim.</p>

      <h2 id="what-announced" class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-8 mb-4">What RackNerd Announced on November 8</h2>
      <p>I opened LowEndBox on the morning of November 9 and found raindog308's post from the day before: <strong>RackNerd's Fall 2026 giveaway is live</strong>, and the prize pool is unusually good for a community provider promotion. Here's the full list:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li><strong>1x Meta Quest 3 512GB VR headset</strong></li>
        <li><strong>1x Synology DS225+ 2-bay NAS</strong></li>
        <li><strong>2x Acer Nitro MG275U 27" gaming monitors</strong></li>
        <li><strong>5x RackNerd KVM VPS</strong> — 4GB RAM, 3 vCPU, 60GB SSD, 7TB monthly transfer. First year free, then renews at $59.99/yr. No obligation to continue.</li>
        <li><strong>10x $50 RackNerd account credit</strong></li>
      </ul>
      <p>No purchase necessary. The entry form runs through <strong>November 30, 2026</strong>. LowEndTalk members whose accounts were at least 30 days old as of November 1 can PM @giveaway with the word <strong>PUMPKIN</strong> to get a secret bonus code worth 100 extra entries — that's up to an 8x chance multiplier over non-community entries.</p>
      <p>I checked the LowEndTalk side too. The forum is behind Cloudflare's JavaScript challenge, so I couldn't verify the bonus-code thread directly. But the mechanism is consistent with RackNerd's previous giveaways (the AdminBolt partnership earlier this year used the same LET-PM-for-bonus-codes pattern), and the LowEndBox post is from their established community writer raindog308.</p>

      <h2 id="vps-deals" class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-8 mb-4">The VPS Deals: $21.99 to $89.99 Per Year</h2>
      <p>The giveaway is the headline, but the accompanying VPS price drops are the part most buyers care about. I pulled every plan spec from the LowEndBox post and cross-referenced them against RackNerd's standard rates listed on our own <a href="/vps/racknerd" class="text-orange-500 hover:text-orange-400">RackNerd review</a>:</p>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto my-6">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-white/10 text-left">
              <th class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-400">Plan</th>
              <th class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-400">Fall 2026 Price</th>
              <th class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-400">vCPU / RAM / SSD</th>
              <th class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-400">Transfer</th>
              <th class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-400">Standard Rate</th>
              <th class="py-2 pr-4 text-gray-400">You Save</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="text-gray-300">
            <tr class="border-b border-white/5">
              <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium text-white">1 GB KVM</td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-green-400"><strong>$21.99/yr</strong></td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4">1 / 1GB / 20GB</td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4">3 TB</td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4">$23.88/yr ($1.99/mo)</td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-green-400">~8%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-white/5">
              <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium text-white">2 GB KVM</td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-green-400"><strong>$35.99/yr</strong></td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4">2 / 2GB / 35GB</td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4">5 TB</td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4">~$39/yr (typical promo)</td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-green-400">~8%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-white/5">
              <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium text-white">4 GB KVM</td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-green-400"><strong>$59.99/yr</strong></td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4">3 / 4GB / 60GB</td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4">7 TB</td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4">~$59-63/yr (typical promo)</td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-green-400">~0-6%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-white/5">
              <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium text-white">6 GB KVM</td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-green-400"><strong>$89.99/yr</strong></td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4">6 / 6GB / 100GB</td>
